# SemText npl-flag — one runtime flag row, six render states
# Direction A "Slate Console" (house style shared with the other tag prompts).
# npl-flag is the ONE interactive npl runtime element in the flags family:
# the row itself is the apply control — a toggle button (role="button",
# aria-pressed, focusable, Enter/Space or click). Its "display modes" are
# the states its schema and vocabulary CSS promise: default, hover/press
# affordance, invalid value, applied, in-container, JS-off. One example
# panel per mode, one frame.
#
# MODE 1 — default flag row (canonical, dark):
#   visible: one quiet rectangular row, thin slate hairline border, rounded
#     corners, transparent (page-surface) fill; a muted monospace name label
#     on the left ("calm_factor"), an " = " separator, then the value
#     ("0.5") in the page foreground, tabular-numeric weight.
#   must never: occlude the value, dim it under an overlay, or replace it
#     with a chip — occlusion belongs to sem-spoiler/the quiz tier, never
#     to npl-flag; render the name and value in different typefaces.
# MODE 2 — hover / keyboard focus:
#   visible: the same row with the hairline border tinted toward the accent
#     (hover) or a 2px accent outline just outside the row (focus-visible);
#     pointer cursor on hover; NOTHING moves — no scale, no slide, no glow
#     bloom. The layout in mode 2 is pixel-identical to mode 1.
#   must never: animate (the element is display-only motion-free); show a
#     focus ring only on click (focus-visible is a keyboard affordance).
# MODE 3 — invalid value (out-of-range or non-numeric):
#   visible: the value span carries a soft amber tint behind it and a small
#     "⚠ " glyph in amber BEFORE the value; the value text itself stays in
#     the page foreground, fully readable — a warning, never an error.
#   must never: red or danger styling, strikethrough, truncated or hidden
#     value, an error dialog look, a thrown/exception presentation.
# MODE 4 — applied state:
#   visible: the row border tinted toward the correct green, and a static
#     " ✓" glyph in the correct green AFTER the value; everything else
#     identical to mode 1. The state reads as calmly completed, not as a
#     success banner.
#   must never: fill the row green, animate the check, confetti, or change
#     the value text.
# MODE 5 — inside the npl-flags container:
#   visible: two flag rows stacked inside the preset-badged npl-flags card
#     (that container's own chrome is the npl-flags lane's); each row keeps
#     its mode-1 anatomy and stays individually click-to-apply.
#   must never: merge the rows into one block; style the container here;
#     let a row's border touch the card edge.
# MODE 6 — JS-off (vocabulary-only, light theme):
#   visible: the authored source rendered as ordinary light-theme prose in
#     a plain light card — attributes are NOT rendered (name/value live in
#     markup), so the row area is empty prose, no border box, no chrome.
#   must never: show any flag row, badge, focus ring, or loading state in
#     the JS-off panel.
#
# Reference snapshots (dark reference page, source views — content and copy
# authority): .tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-flag/npl-flag-fullpage-1280.png
# and npl-flag-ex7-source-1280.png. Per-example crops there are degraded by a
# sticky-header capture artifact; the full-page shot is the good one.
schema: '0.4'
id: reference-npl-flag
type: image
quality: high
service: gemini
model: gemini-2.5-flash-image

prompt:
  text: |
    Dark-mode UI mockup of six reference-page panels in a three-by-two grid,
    wide 16:9, flat technical illustration (screenshot-like, not 3D),
    illustrating one interactive runtime flag row and its six render states.
    Dark slate navy background (#0F172A) with a barely visible thin grid and
    a faint blue radial glow upper-left. Each panel is a dark slate card
    (#1E293B) with a thin slate hairline border (#334155), rounded corners,
    a deep soft shadow, and a small dim caption bar above it; panels are
    separated by thin slate hairlines.

    Every flag row, in every dark panel, has the same anatomy: a full-width
    quiet rectangle with a 1px slate border and 8px rounded corners, transparent
    fill; inside, left-aligned, a muted slate-blue monospace name label
    (#94A3B8, e.g. "calm_factor"), then " = " in the same muted tone, then the
    value (e.g. "0.5") in near-white (#E2E8F0), slightly heavier weight,
    tabular figures. Generous padding; the row reads as a settings row, not a
    button pill.

    PANEL 1 (top-left, caption "default"): one flag row exactly as described,
    at rest.
    PANEL 2 (caption "hover + focus"): two stacked rows — the first with its
    border tinted blue (#60A5FA mixed into the hairline) and a pointer cursor
    nearby; the second identical but with a 2px blue outline offset just
    outside the row. Nothing scaled or moved.
    PANEL 3 (caption "invalid value"): the row as in panel 1, but behind the
    value a soft amber tint (#FBBF24 at low opacity, rounded) and a small
    amber "⚠ " glyph immediately before the value; the value text stays
    near-white and fully readable.
    PANEL 4 (caption "applied"): the row border tinted green (#34D399 mixed
    into the hairline) and a small static green " ✓" immediately after the
    value; value text unchanged, near-white.
    PANEL 5 (caption "inside npl-flags"): a slate card containing a small
    pill badge at top-left, then two flag rows as in panel 1 stacked with
    small gaps, then one line of muted italic note text; the card is the
    container, the rows stay separate rectangles.
    PANEL 6 (caption "JS-off (light)"): a LIGHT panel — near-white card
    (#FAFAFA) with a light hairline border and the authored flag markup as
    plain grey prose lines, no row rectangles, no badge, no chrome; the only
    light panel in the grid.

    Typography: clean grotesque UI sans for captions and prose, monospace for
    all flag names and values. Palette strictly slate navy + slate borders +
    blue accent (#60A5FA) + amber warning (#FBBF24) + green correct (#34D399)
    + near-white text; nothing else. Flat, crisp, high-DPI, no perspective.

    No text other than the labelled names/values and caption words listed.
  negative: text walls, watermark, logo, signature, photorealism, 3D bevels,
    gradients heavier than the stated tints, drop shadows harsher than soft,
    red error styling, strikethrough text, hidden or blurred value text,
    confetti, motion blur, loading spinners, extra panels, light panels
    except panel 6
  style: flat technical UI illustration, minimal-tech dark documentation
    aesthetic, screenshot-like fidelity, crisp hairline borders

attachments:
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-flag/npl-flag-fullpage-1280.png
    role: reference
    description: live dark reference page for npl-flag — all authored variants,
      source views; copy and variant order authority
  - path: /Users/keithbrings/Work/Space/Noizu/.tmp/semtext-docs-overhaul/snaps/npl-flag/npl-flag-ex7-source-1280.png
    role: reference
    description: the in-container variant (npl-flags with two flags + note text),
      source view

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1536
    height: 864
    aspect_ratio: '16:9'

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.75
  criteria:
    anatomy-consistency:
      weight: 0.25
      description: every dark panel repeats the exact row anatomy — muted mono
        name, " = ", near-white value, hairline border row rectangle
      fail_signals:
        - a panel where the value is occluded, blurred, or replaced by a chip
        - rows rendered as filled buttons or pills
    state-legibility:
      weight: 0.25
      description: invalid reads as amber tint + glyph with readable text;
        applied reads as green border + trailing check; neither reads as error
      fail_signals:
        - red/danger styling, strikethrough, or error dialog look
        - animated or filled success banner
    mode-coverage:
      weight: 0.2
      description: six panels present — default, hover+focus, invalid, applied,
        in-container, JS-off light
      fail_signals:
        - missing or duplicated panel
        - more than one light panel
    motion-discipline:
      weight: 0.15
      description: nothing implies animation — no motion blur, scale, glow bloom
      fail_signals:
        - motion blur, scaling artifacts, bloom glows
    palette-discipline:
      weight: 0.15
      description: slate navy + blue/amber/green accents only; panel 6 light
      fail_signals:
        - off-palette saturated colors
        - extra light panels
  reject_if:
    - any panel occludes or hides the flag value text
    - the invalid state uses red or renders as an error
    - a row is missing its name or value
